# oracle: ELECTRODE madelung in.madelung-pppm-ffield: fully periodic pppm/electrode, fix electrode/conp with ffield yes (finite-field efield along z), symm on
# oracle-inputs: w68elec_au_elyt.data
# oracle-compare: thermo=all atoms=all
# Measured max relative error, engine vs native (thermo rows, final atoms): thermo 6.0e-15, atoms 6.2e-13.
# Measured with native LAMMPS (black box): thermo max relative error 3.9e-8, per-atom 1.4e-7 (engine minus native, step 0); the engine grid choice (no slab) matches native here
# Measured with native LAMMPS (black box): G vector 0.32830878, grid 5 5 32, order 5 (no slab: the engine picks them automatically)
# Measured with native LAMMPS (black box): step 0: pe=138.298554116206 c_qbot=-0.287160348654862 c_qtop=0.287160348654862 f_conp[1]=0 f_conp[2]=1
boundary        p p p
kspace_style    pppm/electrode 1.0e-8
units           real
atom_style      full
pair_style      lj/cut/coul/long 12
read_data       w68elec_au_elyt.data
group           bot type 1
group           top type 2
variable        q atom q
compute         qbot bot reduce sum v_q
compute         qtop top reduce sum v_q
fix             conp bot electrode/conp 0 2 couple top 1 symm on ffield yes
thermo_style    custom step pe c_qbot c_qtop f_conp[1] f_conp[2]
thermo_modify   format float %.15g
run             0
